p=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Complete usable core navigation and fix the sourced per-request read-result correlation responsibility for a narrow deterministic check.',map_path='audit-map.json',sources=sources,question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=[binding],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['src-prefix-test','src-read-output-test','src-transport-loss','src-config-apply','src-rsm-recovery'],answered='Membership application/rejection and snapshot recovery callbacks now connect RSM state to Raft under raftMu; persistence and application boundaries complete representative core navigation. Prefix-confirmation tests preserve individual contexts and sequential end-to-end Raft tests expect readiness context equality. Transport.send and existing test networks permit message loss, so losing the first confirmation round and delivering a later round can exercise prefix release without assuming same-link reordering. These are source-derived construction premises, not observed results.',remaining=['Construct and execute a peer-boundary history that elects a leader, commits its no-op, admits distinct remote reads and drops the earlier heartbeat round before delivering the later round.','Review actual observations against the fixed local correlation requirement; client timeout consequence remains outside the check.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The identified discrepancy is now grounded as an implementation-owned correlation obligation; tests will distinguish the actual publication behavior under admitted history.'))
